.TH "rbc::STRIPELEMENT" 3tcl 0\&.5\&.0 "rbc" "Upgraded Tcl/Tk9\&.0-ready RBC package"
.SH NAME
rbc::STRIPELEMENT - Commands in namespace rbc::STRIPELEMENT
.SH "STRIP ELEMENT STRIPELEMENT OPTIONS"
.PP
This page documents the configuration and behavior of strip elements\&.
.PP
STRIPELEMENT denotes an element whose concrete type is StripElement\&. Strip elements are the default
element type of a stripchart widget:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
stripchart \&.s
\&.s element create signal
.fi
.RE
.PP
The common element operations such as create, configure, activate, closest, bind, and delete are
documented in \fIELEMENT\fP\&.
.PP
Strip elements use the same underlying line-rendering machinery as line elements\&. Their data handling, axis
mapping, pens, smoothing, symbols, error bars, value labels, weights, and styles therefore have the same
semantics as described in \fILINEELEMENT\fP\&.
.SH "DIFFERENCES FROM LINE ELEMENTS"
.PP
A strip element exposes a restricted line-element option set intended for stripchart use\&.
.PP
In particular, the following LINEELEMENT options are not available for strip elements:
.TS
tab(|) box;
l l.
Option| Line-element feature
_
-areabackground | area-fill stipple background
-areaforeground | area-fill foreground
-areapattern| area filling with a solid or stipple pattern
-areatile| tiled area filling
-reduce| screen-space trace reduction
-state| line-element state option
-trace| filtering of increasing/decreasing X trace directions
.TE
.PP
All other options listed below use the same interpretation as the corresponding option on \fILINEELEMENT\fP\&.
.SH DATA
.PP
Strip-element coordinates may be supplied with:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
-x
-y
-xdata
-ydata
-data
.fi
.RE
.PP
For example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.s element create signal -x {0 1 2 3 4} -y {1 4 2 5 3}
.fi
.RE
.PP
Rbc vector names may be used instead of literal coordinate lists:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
vector create time voltage

time set    {0 1 2 3 4}
voltage set {1 4 2 5 3}

\&.s element create signal -x time -y voltage
.fi
.RE
.PP
The same transactional and left-to-right data-option semantics described for \fILINEELEMENT\fP apply\&.
.PP
Non-finite data values and values outside the domain of a logarithmic axis form discontinuities in the
rendered trace\&. Points on opposite sides of such a discontinuity are not connected\&.
.SH SMOOTHING
.PP
Strip elements support the same smoothing modes as line elements:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
linear
step
natural
cubic
quadratic
catrom
.fi
.RE
.PP
linear is the default\&.
.PP
Spline smoothing operates in mapped screen coordinates\&. Natural, quadratic, and Catmull-Rom smoothing require
at least three mapped points\&.
.PP
As with line elements, spline smoothing is not allowed to bridge a discontinuity\&. If a discontinuity is
present, the current implementation falls back to ordinary linear trace segments instead of constructing
independent splines for each continuous run\&.
.SH "PENS AND SYMBOLS"
.PP
Strip elements use line pens\&.
.PP
The built-in normal pen can be configured directly with options such as:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
-color
-linewidth
-dashes
-offdash
-fill
-outline
-outlinewidth
-pixels
-symbol
.fi
.RE
.PP
A separately created line pen may be selected with -pen:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.s pen create tracePen -type line -color blue -linewidth 2
\&.s element configure signal -pen tracePen
.fi
.RE
.PP
-activepen selects the pen used when the element or individual data points are active\&.
.PP
See \fILINEELEMENT\fP for detailed descriptions of line pens, symbols, symbol scaling, and symbol-density control\&.
.SH "ERROR BARS"
.PP
Strip elements support the same symmetric and asymmetric error-bar data as line elements:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
-xerror
-xlow
-xhigh
-yerror
-ylow
-yhigh
.fi
.RE
.PP
Their appearance is controlled by:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
-showerrorbars
-errorbarcolor
-errorbarwidth
-errorbarcap
.fi
.RE
.PP
See \fILINEELEMENT\fP for the complete error-bar semantics\&.
.SH "VALUE LABELS"
.PP
Strip elements can display coordinate values next to their data points using -showvalues\&.
.PP
Label appearance is controlled by:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
-valueanchor
-valuecolor
-valuefont
-valueformat
-valuerotate
-valueshadow
.fi
.RE
.PP
See \fILINEELEMENT\fP for value-selection and formatting behavior\&.
.SH "WEIGHTS AND STYLES"
.PP
-weights supplies a numeric weight for each data point and -styles maps weight ranges to named line pens\&.
.PP
The syntax and precedence rules are identical to those described for \fILINEELEMENT\fP\&.
.SH "STRIP ELEMENT OPTIONS"
.PP
The complete strip-element option set is:
.TS
tab(|) box;
l l.
Option| Description
_
-activepen penName| Selects the line pen used for active elements or active points\&. The default is activeLine; an empty value disables the separate active pen\&.
-bindtags tags| Specifies additional graph binding tags for the element\&. The default is all\&.
-color color| Sets the built-in normal pen's trace color\&.
-dashes dashes| Sets the built-in normal pen's trace dash pattern\&. An empty value selects a solid line\&.
-data data| Supplies an even-length list of alternating X and Y values\&.
-errorbarcap width| Sets the error-bar cap width\&.
-errorbarcolor color| Sets the error-bar color\&. defcolor uses the trace color\&.
-errorbarwidth width| Sets the error-bar line width\&.
-fill color| Sets the symbol fill color\&. defcolor uses the trace color; an empty value leaves symbols unfilled\&.
-hide boolean| Controls whether the element is displayed\&.
-label text| Sets the element label used by the legend\&. The initial label is the element name\&.
-labelrelief relief| Sets the relief used for the element's legend label\&.
-linewidth width| Sets the built-in normal pen's trace width\&. A value of 0 suppresses the connecting trace\&.
-mapx axisName| Selects the X axis used to map the element\&. The default is x\&.
-mapy axisName| Selects the Y axis used to map the element\&. The default is y\&.
-maxsymbols number| Controls symbol display density\&. 0 displays all eligible symbols\&.
-offdash color| Sets the color of gaps in dashed traces\&. An empty value leaves the gaps transparent\&.
-outline color| Sets the symbol outline color\&. defcolor uses the trace color\&.
-outlinewidth width| Sets the symbol outline width\&.
-pen penName| Selects a named line pen as the normal pen\&. An empty value selects the built-in pen\&.
-pixels size| Sets the requested symbol size\&.
-scalesymbols boolean | Controls automatic symbol-size scaling as axis ranges change\&.
-showerrorbars value| Selects which X and/or Y error bars are drawn\&.
-showvalues value| Selects which coordinate values are displayed next to data points\&.
-smooth mode| Selects linear, step, natural, cubic, quadratic, or catrom smoothing\&.
-styles styles| Maps ranges of per-point weights to named line pens\&.
-symbol symbol| Selects the point symbol\&.
-valueanchor anchor| Sets the anchor of data-value labels\&.
-valuecolor color| Sets the data-value label color\&.
-valuefont font| Sets the data-value label font\&.
-valueformat format| Sets the validated floating-point format used for data-value labels\&.
-valuerotate angle| Sets the rotation angle of data-value labels\&.
-valueshadow shadow| Sets the optional shadow for data-value labels\&.
-weights values| Supplies per-point numeric weights used by -styles\&.
-x values| Supplies X coordinates as a Tcl list or Rbc vector\&.
-xdata values| Synonym for -x\&.
-xerror values| Supplies symmetric X error magnitudes\&.
-xhigh values| Supplies absolute upper X error-bar coordinates\&.
-xlow values| Supplies absolute lower X error-bar coordinates\&.
-y values| Supplies Y coordinates as a Tcl list or Rbc vector\&.
-ydata values| Synonym for -y\&.
-yerror values| Supplies symmetric Y error magnitudes\&.
-yhigh values| Supplies absolute upper Y error-bar coordinates\&.
-ylow values| Supplies absolute lower Y error-bar coordinates\&.
.TE

